{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03094",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 4.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "hello? Doctor? I was told to come in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.93,
      "end_seconds": 11.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Okay, yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.55,
      "end_seconds": 20.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "So the thing is, um, I've got a high sugar test in pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.41,
      "end_seconds": 24.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.98,
      "end_seconds": 29.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "It's been going on for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.37,
      "end_seconds": 34.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.37,
      "end_seconds": 40.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I'd give it a seven, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.9,
      "end_seconds": 43.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.43,
      "end_seconds": 57.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.01,
      "text": "It usually comes with no symptoms. I've also had a big baby on the scan. The no symptoms? That's been for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.55,
      "end_seconds": 66.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.96,
      "end_seconds": 78.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "okay, this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.24,
      "end_seconds": 106.15,
      "duration_seconds": 15.91,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 74 beats a minute, temperature is 36.5 degrees, height 186 centimetres, pressure 108 over 73, BMI works out to 21.1, weight 73 kilos, oxygen saturation is 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.55,
      "end_seconds": 110.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.32,
      "end_seconds": 115.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.13,
      "end_seconds": 133.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Your blood pressure is normal and your urine has no sugar today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.33,
      "end_seconds": 153.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.25,
      "end_seconds": 162.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. And passing a lot of urine, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.1,
      "end_seconds": 167.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "no passing a lot of urine, thankfully"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.57,
      "end_seconds": 173.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "have you had any thirst, reduced baby movements or blurred vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.21,
      "end_seconds": 176.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.4,
      "end_seconds": 178.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.07,
      "end_seconds": 182.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.42,
      "end_seconds": 198.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Okay, any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.02,
      "end_seconds": 201.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.56,
      "end_seconds": 218.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "do you follow any particular diet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.93,
      "end_seconds": 226.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I'm vegetarian and have been for years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.37,
      "end_seconds": 229.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.49,
      "end_seconds": 234.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.21,
      "end_seconds": 240.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.4,
      "end_seconds": 253.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.54,
      "text": "Heart failure, for about ten years. I have an irregular heartbeat, for two years. I have an enlarged prostate, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.44,
      "end_seconds": 269.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Right, yes, an irregular heartbeat is known to us, good to have that clear. Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.38,
      "end_seconds": 276.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "I had a cataract operation in my left eye about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.98,
      "end_seconds": 280.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.21,
      "end_seconds": 299.08,
      "duration_seconds": 17.87,
      "text": "Spironolactone. I take it 25 milligrams, once a day. Warfarin, 3 milligrams, in the evening. Uh, I'm supposed to take it regularly, but I don't always manage. Tamsulosin. I take it 0.4 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.81,
      "end_seconds": 304.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.39,
      "end_seconds": 308.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "no, it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.38,
      "end_seconds": 348.02,
      "duration_seconds": 38.64,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: The most likely explanation is gestational diabetes controllable with diet. I'll request a glucose meter and diary, it'll help with gestational diabetes. We should do a growth scan for gestational diabetes. Replace sugary drinks and white starches with wholegrains and walk after meals. I think the diabetes midwife should see you too. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.55,
      "end_seconds": 356.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Let's review you in two weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.28,
      "end_seconds": 360.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "thank you, that's helpful"
    }
  ]
}